Version 2.24, July 8, 1994

6/27/94 required_buffer_size parameter on decode_identifier

There is now a required_buffer_size parameter in decode_identifier,
which returns the buffer size needed.  That is useful when a buffer
overflow occurs (it tells you how big a buffer must be allocated to
try again).

6/10/94 Changes in command line handling

The eccp script has been changed to accommodate the same command line
changes that were made in the front end.

In addition to the changes described for the front end, eccp now uses
the -O option to specify that the C compiler used to compile the
generated code should be invoked with optimization requested.

The -g option no longer causes the .int.c file to be retained.
A separate option (-k or --keep_gen_c) is now available to
request that the .int.c file be preserved.

The -gn option (which was equivalent to the new -g --keep_int_c) has been
eliminated.

The --driver_debug option has been added to display, for debugging
purposes, the commands executed by the driver.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.23, May 25, 1994

4/11/94 edg_prelink displays identifiers in demangled form

edg_demangle now calls decode_identifier and displays identifiers
in decoded format.  The -m option can be used to display the
names in the old mangled format.

4/11/94 edg_prelink allows substitution in error strings

edg_prelink now provides a simple text insertion facility to
insert variable information in error messages.

4/5/94  eccp uses edg_decode to demangle the names in linker output

The eccp script has been modified to use edg_decode to demangle
names in the output of the linker.

4/5/94  Name demangler

A name demangler has been added.  The code is contained in decode.c,
and a filter program that uses the code is in edg_decode.c.

3/18/94 -L and -l options now supported by edg_prelink

The -L and -l linker options are now passed from eccp to the prelinker so
that the prelinker can include the libraries specified by the -l options
when determining which templates need to be instantiated.

3/17/94 Command line option change

The -l (don't limit recursion) option has been renamed to -r.  This has
been changed to allow the use of the -l option to specify library names.

3/1/94  Changes to facilitate error message catalogs

edg_prelink.c has been modified to simplify the task of using
a message catalog for the storage of error messages.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.22, February 26, 1994

2/21/94  Display of underlying C compiler diagnostics

Output from the underlying C compiler is bracketed by special messages
from eccp so that the source of the messages is more clear.  This
change was motivated by the fact that the C generating back end now
issues #line directives so the file name used by the C compiler in
diagnostics is now the original source file name instead of the
.int.c file name.

2/9/94   Purify option

The "-purify" option has been added to eccp.  This allows you to link
programs with purify.

1/17/94  Portability issues

edg_munch incorrectly used a char as the return value of getc.  edg_munch
and edg_prelink failed to cast the argument of isalpha to unsigned char.
These have been fixed.

edg_prelink.h no longer explicitly declares popen().  The declaration
from stdio.h is now used.

fclose was being called to close a file even when the open failed.  This
has been corrected.

1/5/94   Version of getopt routine now provided

The utility programs now provide their own version of the getopt
routine for use on systems that do not provide a getopt.

1/5/94   Temporary directory used by eccp

The eccp script now uses the environment variable TMPDIR as the temporary
directory.  If TMPDIR is not set, /tmp is used.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.21, December 21, 1993

12/16/93 Change in name of prelinker options

The nm format option for Solaris has been changed from SVR4 to Solaris
because we learned that the Solaris format is actually different from
the standard SVR4 format.

The M88K option has been renamed to SVR4 because it more closely matches
the standard SVR4 nm output.

12/14/93 Command line information in .ii file in preprocessing mode

The eccp script no longer updates the command line information in the .ii
file when invoked with options that cause the compiler to be
executed in preprocessing mode (i.e., -P, -E, -H, -M).

11/15/93 Prelinker problem with eliminated instantiation sites

Under some conditions the prelinker failed to reassign an instantiation
after the current instantiation site has been changed in such a way
that the instantiation can no longer be generated.  This has been fixed.

11/15/93 Aborting compilations that are executed by the prelinker

If a compilation is aborted while the prelinker is recompiling a file
(but before the new object file has been created) an application may
be left in a state in which simply typing "make" will not result
in a the application being successfully built.  The user would need to
either remove the .o file or touch the .c file and rerun make.
This problem has been solved by having the prelinker remove the .o
file before recompiling a file.
